<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-running-code">
  <title>Running Code in This Book</title>

  <p>This book has code boxes you can run right on the page.
  Click a <q>Try It</q> title to open its code box. Press <term>Save &amp; Run</term> to run the code.
  What the code prints shows up below the box.
  You can change the code and run it again as many times as you like.
  Your browser saves your code each time you run it, so it is still there when you come back on the same computer.</p>

  <activity xml:id="try-first-program">
    <title>Hello, World</title>
    <program xml:id="ac-first-program" interactive="activecode" language="javascript">
      <code>
console.log("Hello, World!");
      </code>
    </program>
  </activity>

  <p>Open the <q>Try It</q> box above, change the message inside the quotes, and press <term>Save &amp; Run</term> again.</p>

  <exercise xml:id="mc-running-code" label="mc-running-code">
    <statement>
      <p>Where does the output of <c>console.log</c> show up in this book?</p>
    </statement>
    <choices>
      <choice correct="yes">
        <statement><p>Below the code box, after you press Save &amp; Run.</p></statement>
        <feedback><p>Right. The output shows up below the box.</p></feedback>
      </choice>
      <choice>
        <statement><p>In a new browser tab.</p></statement>
        <feedback><p>No. Everything stays on this page.</p></feedback>
      </choice>
      <choice>
        <statement><p>Nowhere. The code only runs when you save the page.</p></statement>
        <feedback><p>No. The code runs when you press Save &amp; Run.</p></feedback>
      </choice>
    </choices>
  </exercise>
</section>
